+# v0.12 — Control as a shift in responsibility
+
+Requested 2026-09-15. Fixed comparison: `.build/revision_0_12_baseline/manifest.json` (verified v0.11).
+
+- Delete slide 6 Hi Robot quantitative page, keeping all three original hierarchy figures on slide 5. Replace slide 6 with one editable responsibility-shift diagram, keeping 38 pages and chapter numbering stable.
+- Earlier design hypothesis: System 2 sends semantic/subtask information. System 1, a steerable generalist VLA/WAM policy π(a | o,l), is expected to supply broad visuomotor generalization. “Arbitrary” inputs are an aspiration, not a demonstrated guarantee.
+- Emerging pattern: foundation-model/Agent System 2 can take on more spatial grounding, action selection and parameterization. System 1 may supply narrower action primitives, with Controller/local servo still present. This is partial migration, not all dynamics/high-frequency feedback moving into an LLM.
+- System labels are functional shorthand for this talk; analytic tools are not all learned System 1 neural policies. Direct/Hybrid/tool implementations remain distinct.
+- Robot-data training is a plausible framing/conditional hypothesis; Astra training recipe and causal attribution are not disclosed. Do not present a proven training-data cause, universal primitive sufficiency, or all-task superiority.
+- Make Chinese narration and chapter transitions follow this spine: design hypothesis → older model/interface evidence → organizing primitives → stronger Agent evidence → remaining control gaps. Preserve English slides, original styling, videos, source boundaries and quantitative results elsewhere.
+- Main deliverable remains self-contained HTML plus synchronized Chinese script. Rebuild, refresh CJK subset, audit layout/UI/playback and visual diagram, independent Standards/Spec review.
+- No new external research claims, model calls, release/push or legacy PPTX/PDF/ZIP regeneration.
+
+## Visual follow-up
+
+The user rejected the initial diagram as wordy. Compress slide 6 into two sparse control chains: short role labels, generalist policy formula, a single transfer arrow and an area/color shift from System 1 to System 2. Move explanatory detail into the Chinese narration. Retain semantic accuracy and original fonts; do not weaken the source/causal caveats in narration.
+
+Latest naming correction: the two slide-6 endpoints are labeled **Controller** only, without System 0 / Servo. Preserve original terminology inside the unedited slide-5 source figures.
